 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "Laundry is the washing, drying and ironing of clothes and household linen; the word also means the place where this is done.\nTypes of laundry:\n• home (domestic) laundry: done at home by hand or with a washing machine;\n• on-premises (in-house) laundry: inside an institution that washes its own linen — hotels, hospitals, boarding schools;\n• commercial laundry: a business (pressing, dry cleaner) that washes and irons clothes for customers for payment.\nSteps: sort clothes (whites, colours, delicate), check pockets, read care labels, remove stains, wash with detergent, rinse well, dry (in the sun or shade), iron and fold.\nDry cleaning uses chemical solvents instead of water, for delicate fabrics.",
  "checks": []
 },
 "worked_example": {
  "status": "draft",
  "vars": {},
  "problem": "Why should white and coloured clothes be washed separately?",
  "steps": [
   "Some coloured clothes lose dye in water.",
   "The dye can stain the white clothes."
  ],
  "answer": "So that colours do not run onto white clothes.",
  "checks": []
 },
